---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.author}.`}>
	<h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-3xl">About</h1>
	<div class="prose dark:prose-invert mt-6 max-w-none">
		<p>
			Hi, I'm David — an Azure Cloud Architect at glueckkanja AG, based in
			Bavaria, Germany. Over the last several years I've focused on the
			unglamorous but essential part of the stack: building the data
			foundation — pulling scattered sources into a single lakehouse,
			structuring it, cleaning it up, and making it something teams can
			actually build on.
		</p>
		<p>
			These days that foundation is what makes real AI work — LLMs, agents,
			and automation that hold up outside a demo instead of hallucinating on
			messy inputs. This blog is where I write about that intersection:
			practical, customer-facing lessons from real Azure data &amp; AI
			engagements, not theory. (Colleagues call me Data Dave — now you know
			where the name comes from.) Opinions here are my own, not my
			employer's.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
